{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2722","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2722","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2722\",\"parent_revision\":\"9cd9e5dbd75ee9d31b98d32f97cfc6de4e08e77605e1ff4fe60f4a2610e6c4a2\",\"root_revision\":\"9cd9e5dbd75ee9d31b98d32f97cfc6de4e08e77605e1ff4fe60f4a2610e6c4a2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: 2026-07-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nCURRENT STATE: The skill-creator authoring guidance offers no pattern for defending workflow-enforcing skills against agents skipping steps. The \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" section of plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md (lines 101-166) lists only frontmatter + body + bundled resources, and the pre-publish authoring-checklist (plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/authoring-checklist.md) has no item for a \\\"Common Rationalizations\\\" or \\\"Red Flags\\\" section. Grep of both files for \\\"rationalization\\\" and \\\"red flag\\\" returns zero matches. The repo's process-discipline concerns (agents defaulting to the shortest path and skipping verification, quality gates, and reproduction) are enforced only ad hoc in CLAUDE.md and rules, never as a reusable authored skill component.\\n\\nSOURCE PATTERN (Agent Skills, addyosmani/agent-skills, research entry Key Features > Consistent Skill Anatomy): every skill embeds a \\\"Common Rationalizations\\\" table of excuses agents use to skip steps (e.g. \\\"I'll add tests later\\\") paired with documented counter-arguments, plus a \\\"Red Flags\\\" section of signs something is wrong. Research quote: \\\"Every skill includes a table of common excuses agents use to skip steps ... with documented counter-arguments.\\\"\\n\\nTARGET STATE: skill-creator documents an optional \\\"anti-rationalization\\\" component for workflow-enforcing skills \u2014 a two-column table (Rationalization | Counter-argument) plus an optional Red Flags list \u2014 with a short authoring rule for when to include it (skills that enforce a multi-step discipline with skippable quality gates). The pre-publish authoring-checklist gains a checklist item covering it. Observable: grep -i \\\"rationalization\\\" over plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/ returns matches in both SKILL.md (or a references file it links) and authoring-checklist.md.\\n\\nMEASURABLE SIGNAL: (1) authoring-checklist.md contains a checkbox line referencing an anti-rationalization / Common Rationalizations section for workflow-enforcing skills; (2) skill-creator SKILL.md or a linked references file documents the two-column table shape with at least one concrete example row; (3) grep -ri \\\"rationalization\\\" plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/ is non-empty.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:04:37.486206Z</sub>\\n\\n\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:06:18.084234Z</sub>\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Concerns\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\nThe addition of an optional anti-rationalization component (Rationalization | Response table + Red Flags subsection) to skill-creator authoring guidance aligns with three core mission dimensions:\\n\\n**1. Skill-Creator Mission:** skill-creator's purpose is to \\\"guide effective skill creation\\\" with focus on \\\"concise is key\\\" and progressive disclosure patterns. Adding a structured pattern to prevent agent workflow-skipping enhances skill effectiveness without expanding scope \u2014 the pattern is optional and applies only to workflow-enforcing skills.\\n\\n**2. Development Harness Design Principle:** The harness explicitly owns \\\"process discipline\\\" (Development Harness CLAUDE.md, lines 38-39). The item notes: \\\"The repo's process-discipline concerns... are enforced only ad hoc in CLAUDE.md and rules, never as a reusable authored skill component.\\\" The proposed change embeds this discipline as a reusable component, advancing the stated design goal.\\n\\n**3. .claude/CLAUDE.md Standards:** The project standard emphasizes \\\"Standard of Excellence\\\" (line 52) and \\\"Evidence-Action Proportionality\\\" (file `evidence-action-proportionality.md`). Adding guardrails against rationalization (\\\"should work now\\\", \\\"I'm confident\\\", \\\"Linter passed so build passes\\\") directly implements these standards within skill guidance.\\n\\n**In-Repository Precedent:** The pattern already exists in production within `/dh:verify-done` SKILL.md (Section 7: \\\"Rationalization Prevention\\\", lines 169-183). This constitutes a merged implementation establishing internal direction.\\n\\n**External Alignment:** Item cites SOURCE PATTERN from agent-skills research (addyosmani/agent-skills): \\\"every skill embeds a 'Common Rationalizations' table... with documented counter-arguments.\\\" The proposed change brings internal skill-creator into alignment with established best practice.\\n\\n**Design Impact:** Optional scope, targeted application (workflow-enforcing skills only), and reusable pattern \u2014 no mission expansion or scope creep detected.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add anti-rationalization table pattern to skill-creator authoring guidance** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/skill-generation-tools/agent-skills.md \u2014 pattern: Anti-rationalization / Common Rationalizations table (Consistent Skill Anatomy)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-07-07\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:2793b6e755274f858b1438a3bc57d4e6 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-07-10)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T07:59:53.086491Z</sub>\\n\\nN/A for feature items \u2014 this is a documentation/authoring-guidance addition, not a bug fix. There is no failing behavior to reproduce. The absence of the pattern is confirmed by: `grep -ri \\\"rationalization\\\" plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` returning zero matches (verified during RT-ICA, condition #2).\\n</div>\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:00:04.679115Z</sub>\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 P1 per backlog metadata. Not blocking any in-flight work, but it closes a known gap (zero existing anti-rationalization guidance in skill-creator) that the kaizen-improvement pipeline already delegates skill-content-improvement work through (`plugins/agentskill-kaizen/skills/kaizen-improvement/references/improvement-templates.md`), so shipping it raises the quality floor for every skill generated downstream of that pipeline going forward. No hard deadline; risk is documentation drift/inconsistency (two similarly-shaped tables with different column names) if left ungroomed longer.\\n\\nEffort: S \u2014 two file edits (one new references file + one linked pointer in SKILL.md's Anatomy of a Skill section, plus one checklist line in authoring-checklist.md), scope and placement already fully resolved by the user Decision entry, no code changes, no test suite changes.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:00:16.380189Z</sub>\\n\\n- Blocks: No in-flight work is blocked. This is additive authoring guidance.\\n- Bottleneck: Every skill authored or reviewed via `plugin-creator:skill-creator` \u2014 including those generated by the `kaizen-improvement` pipeline's delegation to `subagent_type=\\\"plugin-creator:skill-creator\\\"` (`plugins/agentskill-kaizen/skills/kaizen-improvement/references/improvement-templates.md` line 87) and skills built via `.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md`'s \\\"follows skill-creator guidelines\\\" gate (line 130) \u2014 currently has no documented pattern for defending a workflow-enforcing skill against agents rationalizing their way past skippable quality gates.\\n- Terminology risk if shipped without reconciliation: `plugins/development-harness/skills/verify-done/SKILL.md` (lines 169-186) already ships a `Rationalization | Response` table under a \\\"Rationalization Prevention\\\" heading; `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agentskills/references/best-practices.md` (lines 476-480) already ships a differently-scoped `Anti-pattern | Problem | Instead` \\\"Anti-Patterns to Avoid\\\" table linked from the same SKILL.md section being edited. Both are Impact Radius findings (MEDIUM risk each) that acceptance criteria must guard against.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:00:27.946200Z</sub>\\n\\n- Gives skill authors (human and agent) a documented, reusable component for defending workflow-enforcing skills against agents rationalizing skipped steps, sourced from a verified external pattern (addyosmani/agent-skills, Consistent Skill Anatomy).\\n- Establishes a single canonical column-naming convention (`Rationalization | Response`) across the repo instead of leaving `verify-done`'s existing instance as an unreferenced one-off.\\n- Adds a checklist gate (`authoring-checklist.md`) so future workflow-enforcing skills are prompted to consider this component during pre-publish review, rather than relying on ad hoc inclusion.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:00:39.193286Z</sub>\\n\\nAn agent or human using `plugin-creator:skill-creator` to author a workflow-enforcing skill (one that encodes a multi-step discipline with skippable quality gates) is guided, via SKILL.md's \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" section and a linked references file, to include a two-column `Rationalization | Response` table (naming excuses an executing agent might give for skipping a step, paired with the counter-response) plus an optional \\\"Red Flags\\\" subsection beneath it. The pre-publish authoring-checklist presents this as a checkbox item so it is checked (or explicitly deemed not applicable) before a workflow-enforcing skill ships. The guidance and its worked example use the same column vocabulary already shipped in `plugins/development-harness/skills/verify-done/SKILL.md` (`Rationalization | Response`), so an author cross-referencing both files sees one consistent pattern rather than two divergent ones. The guidance is distinguishable in intent from the existing \\\"Anti-Patterns to Avoid\\\" table in `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agentskills/references/best-practices.md` (which addresses mistakes in constructing the skill file, not excuses an agent gives while executing it).\\n</div>\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:01:50.561025Z</sub>\\n\\n1. `grep -ri \\\"rationalization\\\" plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` returns non-empty output, with at least one match inside `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/authoring-checklist.md` and at least one match inside `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md` or a references file it links via markdown link syntax (`[text](./references/....md)`).\\n2. `authoring-checklist.md` contains a checkbox line (`- [ ] ...`) referencing an anti-rationalization / Common Rationalizations (or equivalently-named) section for workflow-enforcing skills, formatted consistently with the file's existing checkbox-under-section-header convention.\\n3. The new references file (or the SKILL.md section, if inlined) documents a two-column table using the header `Rationalization | Response` \u2014 matching the column vocabulary already shipped in `plugins/development-harness/skills/verify-done/SKILL.md` lines 169-186 \u2014 not `Rationalization | Counter-argument`. `grep -F \\\"Rationalization | Response\\\"` against the new content returns a match.\\n4. The table includes at least one concrete example row (a specific rationalization phrase paired with a specific response), not a placeholder or generic description of the pattern.\\n5. A Red Flags subsection (or equivalently-named list) appears beneath the table within the same component, per the Decision entry combining both into one authoring-checklist item.\\n6. `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md` line count does not grow beyond a short pointer/link addition to the \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" section \u2014 `wc -l plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md` after the change should not increase by more than a few lines, verifying the bulk of new content landed in the references file per the Decision (placement) rather than inline, avoiding further skilllint SK006/SK007 exposure on an already-585-line file.\\n7. `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/` exits 0 (no new SK006/SK007 token-threshold violations introduced).\\n8. `uv run prek run --files plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/authoring-checklist.md <new-references-file>` passes (markdownlint-cli2 table/list formatting, blank-lines-around-fences, etc.).\\n9. The new content does not reuse or collide with the \\\"Anti-Patterns to Avoid\\\" table structure/heading in `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agentskills/references/best-practices.md` (lines 476-480) \u2014 the new component's heading and surrounding text are distinguishable in scope (agent execution-time rationalizations vs. skill-construction mistakes) from that existing table, so an author reading both is not left to guess which applies.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:01:02.239138Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | plugin-creator:skill-creator |\\n| Prior work (precedent) | plugins/development-harness/skills/verify-done/SKILL.md (Rationalization Prevention, lines 169-186) |\\n| Prior work (adjacent, terminology risk) | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agentskills/references/best-practices.md (Anti-Patterns to Avoid, lines 476-480) |\\n| Prior work (sibling references file) | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/best-practices-upstream.md |\\n| Consumer | plugins/agentskill-kaizen/skills/kaizen-improvement/references/improvement-templates.md (delegates to plugin-creator:skill-creator) |\\n| Consumer | .claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md (line 130, \\\"follows skill-creator guidelines\\\" gate) |\\n| Source pattern | ./research/skill-generation-tools/agent-skills.md (addyosmani/agent-skills, Consistent Skill Anatomy) |\\n| Docs | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/authoring-checklist.md |\\n| CI | .pre-commit-config.yaml (skilllint, markdownlint-cli2 hooks) |\\n| CI | .github/workflows/code-quality.yml |\\n</div>\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:00:50.566062Z</sub>\\n\\nConfirmed to exist (Glob-verified):\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md` \u2014 \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" section, lines 101-166 (585 lines total in file)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/authoring-checklist.md` \u2014 pre-publish checklist, 22 items across 4 sections (Core Quality, Structure, Code and Scripts, Testing)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/` \u2014 directory where the new references file (per user Decision) is placed\\n\\nAdjacent files relevant to scope/terminology reconciliation (not required edit targets per Decision, but named in Impact Radius):\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/verify-done/SKILL.md` (lines 169-186) \u2014 existing `Rationalization | Response` precedent\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agentskills/references/best-practices.md` (lines 476-480) \u2014 existing, differently-scoped \\\"Anti-Patterns to Avoid\\\" table\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/best-practices-upstream.md` \u2014 sibling references file in the same directory\\n</div>\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:01:13.688929Z</sub>\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 RT-ICA verdict APPROVED, all 6 conditions AVAILABLE, no open questions or blocking prerequisites.\\n- Blocks: None directly. Enables (as a natural, larger follow-up, explicitly out of scope for this item per the Impact Radius \\\"Scope expansion\\\" finding) a future retrofit of the pattern into the ~9 files already containing ad hoc Red-Flags/rationalization-style sections (e.g. the three near-duplicate `test-failure-mindset/SKILL.md` copies, `plan-validator.md`, `feature-verifier.md`, `investigation-escalation.md`, `rtfp/SKILL.md`, `instruction-reviewing.md`, `post-completion-validation-protocol.md`) \u2014 do not fold that retrofit into this item's scope.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T08:01:25.319820Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall \u2014 consistent with the Priority section's Effort: S rating.\\n\\n- New references file in `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/` documenting the `Rationalization | Response` table shape with at least one concrete example row, plus optional Red Flags subsection \u2014 1 file.\\n- Short pointer added to SKILL.md's \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" section linking to the new file \u2014 1 edit, no line-budget growth beyond a pointer (avoids compounding the existing 585-line overrun per Impact Radius HIGH-risk finding on SKILL.md).\\n- One new checkbox item in `authoring-checklist.md` covering both the table and the optional Red Flags subsection, formatted per existing checkbox-under-section-header convention (22 existing items, 4 sections).\\n- No code, no tests, no CI config changes expected \u2014 `.pre-commit-config.yaml` and `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` entries are VERIFY_COMPATIBLE only (skilllint token thresholds, markdownlint-cli2 table formatting).\\n</div>\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-10T07:54:30.361487Z</sub>\\n\\nDesign decisions resolved by user (2026-07-10, in-session AskUserQuestion during grooming):\\n\\n1. **Placement**: New references/ file in skill-creator, linked from SKILL.md's \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" section with a short pointer. Rationale: SKILL.md is already 585 lines vs its own 500-line guidance (skilllint SK006/SK007 exposure \u2014 impact-analyst finding).\\n2. **Table shape**: Two-column `Rationalization | Response` \u2014 matches the existing in-repo precedent in dh:verify-done's SKILL.md, keeping one consistent column vocabulary across the repo (supersedes the item description's \\\"Counter-argument\\\" column name; the addyosmani source pattern intent is unchanged).\\n3. **Red Flags**: Documented as part of the same component \u2014 the table plus an optional Red Flags subsection beneath it; a single authoring-checklist item covers both.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/skills/kaizen-improvement/references/improvement-templates.md` - Already covered under Code - Consumers (delegation to skill-creator). | Risk: LOW | Why: see Consumers entry.\\n- `.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md` - Already covered under Code - Consumers (generic guideline-inheritance reference). | Risk: LOW | Why: see Consumers entry.\\n- No agent or skill file was found that restates or duplicates the \\\"Anatomy of a Skill\\\" enumeration or the authoring-checklist item list inline (verified via grep for `authoring-checklist` and `Anatomy of a Skill` across `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/references/`, `agentskill-kaizen`, and `.claude/skills/skill-research-process` \u2014 no matches). This means the ~53 other files that merely reference \\\"skill-creator\\\" by name (routing/delegation mentions in READMEs, insight files, other plugin CLAUDE.md files) do not need updates \u2014 they point at the skill by name, not at its enumerated content, so they cannot go stale from this addition.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `plugins/agentskill-kaizen/skills/kaizen-improvement/references/improvement-templates.md::Delegation Step` (line 87) - Delegates \\\"skill content improvement\\\" tasks to `subagent_type=\\\"plugin-creator:skill-creator\\\"`; this is the actual mechanism (kaizen-improvement pipeline) that generated this very backlog item from the research entry and will execute the eventual fix. | Risk: LOW | Why: delegation contract only names the skill, does not restate its content \u2014 adding a new optional component does not change the delegation contract's shape, so no update is needed; included because it is the direct execution path for this change.\\n- `.claude/skills/skill-research-process/SKILL.md` (line 130, Pre-Requisites checklist: \\\"Skill follows skill-creator guidelines\\\") - Generic reference to skill-creator's authoring guidance as an acceptance gate for skills built via the research-process workflow. | Risk: LOW | Why: statement is generic (\\\"follows skill-creator guidelines\\\") and does not enumerate specific checklist items, so it automatically inherits the new optional component without needing edits; flagged for completeness since it is a real consumer of the guidance being changed.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/best-practices-upstream.md` - Sibling references file linked from SKILL.md (\\\"Upstream best practices... plan-validate-execute\\\") in the same `references/` directory as `authoring-checklist.md` and a plausible alternate placement location for the new component if SKILL.md size forces extraction. | Risk: LOW | Why: no content conflict identified; noted only as a placement-decision-adjacent file, not because it requires a mandatory edit.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/agentskills/references/best-practices.md` (lines 476-480) - Already contains a similarly-shaped 3-column \\\"Anti-Patterns to Avoid\\\" table (`Anti-pattern | Problem | Instead`) and is directly linked from skill-creator SKILL.md Step 5 (\\\"Output formats, examples, anti-patterns, and quality standards\\\"). Terminology overlap between \\\"Anti-Patterns to Avoid\\\" (mistakes in constructing the skill file itself) and the new \\\"anti-rationalization\\\" component (excuses an agent gives when *executing* a produced skill) is a real confusion risk for authors reading both files back to back. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: documentation risk \u2014 two similarly-named/shaped tables serving different purposes, in files linked from the same SKILL.md section, with no existing text distinguishing them.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/verify-done/SKILL.md` (lines 169-186, \\\"Rationalization Prevention\\\" section) - Contains an existing, already-shipped two-column `Rationalization | Response` table plus a \\\"Red flags in your own output\\\" bullet list \u2014 functionally the exact pattern this item proposes to generalize into skill-creator's authoring guidance, but with a different second-column name (\\\"Response\\\" vs. the item's proposed \\\"Counter-argument\\\"). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: naming divergence between the new canonical guidance and the closest existing real-world instance of the pattern in this repo; if skill-creator's authoring rule uses different column terminology than this precedent, future authors have two inconsistent examples to imitate. Not a required edit target (this file is out of the item's stated scope) but essential prior art to reconcile terminology against.\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md::Anatomy of a Skill` (lines 101-166) - This section is the target location the item names for documenting the two-column Rationalization table + optional Red Flags list and the authoring rule for when to include it. The file is already 585 lines \u2014 well over the 500-line guideline that `authoring-checklist.md` itself enforces (\\\"SKILL.md body is under 500 lines\\\"). Any inline addition here compounds an existing self-violation and risks tripping `skilllint` SK006 (warning)/SK007 (error) token thresholds on the file the pre-commit `skilllint` hook actively gates. | Risk: HIGH | Why: producer file already exceeds its own documented line budget; inline placement of new content risks a structural lint failure at commit time, and progressive-disclosure guidance elsewhere in the same file (`references/` for anything not \\\"truly core\\\") argues against inline placement.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/authoring-checklist.md` - The item explicitly requires a new checklist line here (\\\"gains a checklist item covering it\\\"). This is the second required edit target (Core Quality or a new subsection). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: file is a `references/` doc so it is not `skilllint`-gated (only `SKILL.md`/`CLAUDE.md`/`agents/*.md`/`commands/*.md`/`plugin.json` match the hook's file filter), but it IS covered by the repo-wide `markdownlint-cli2` pre-commit hook and CI `lint-markdown` job \u2014 a malformed table or missing blank lines around it will fail CI.\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-07-15T08:20:12.986228Z</sub>\\n\\n- [x] MINOR (reported by quality-worker, T0 multi-perspective review): SKILL.md:156 heading nesting under \\\"Bundled Resources\\\" \u2014 RESOLVED by T5 (commit f1c5c89), heading retitled to \\\"Bundled Resources and Content Patterns (optional)\\\" to match its actual scope. Recorded as DN-1 (design-refinement) on plan P6f2ba479/T5.\\n- [x] INFO (reported by quality-worker, T0 multi-perspective review) / DN-2 (intent divergence, flagged by T6 context-refinement): authoring-checklist.md had zero inbound links from SKILL.md \u2014 originally marked out-of-scope for #2722 (\\\"Not introduced by this change; flagged for awareness only\\\"). T5 fixed it anyway (added 2 inbound links, commit f1c5c89), exceeding the architect spec's stated file scope. User decision (2026-07-12): ACCEPTED retroactively \u2014 the fix stays, not reverted, not re-filed as a separate item.\\n\\nDN-3 (design-refinement, no review needed): Table Shape/Red Flags examples in anti-rationalization-pattern.md fenced in ```markdown blocks per architect spec, fixed by T5.\\n</div>\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml::skilllint hook` (lines 174-181) - Runs `uvx skilllint@latest check --fix` against files matching `^(plugins|\\\\.claude)/.*(SKILL\\\\.md|CLAUDE\\\\.md|agents/.*\\\\.md|commands/.*\\\\.md|plugin\\\\.json)$` on every commit touching those paths. `skill-creator/SKILL.md` matches this pattern; `authoring-checklist.md` does not (it is a `references/` file, outside the filter). | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: operational exposure \u2014 if the SKILL.md edit pushes token count past `TOKEN_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (SK006) or `TOKEN_ERROR_THRESHOLD` (SK007), the commit-time hook will warn or block, given the file is already 585 lines against a documented 500-line target.\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml::markdownlint-cli2 hook` (lines 113-117) - Applies to all markdown except `plan/`, `.claude/backlog/`, `.claude/BACKLOG.md`, `graphify-out/` \u2014 both `SKILL.md` and `authoring-checklist.md` are in scope. New tables/lists must follow MD031 (blank lines around fences) and standard table syntax. | Risk: LOW | Why: mechanical formatting risk only, standard for any markdown edit in this repo; well-understood gate.\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml::lint-markdown, validate-plugins jobs` (lines 93-105, 141-143) - CI re-runs `markdownlint-cli2 --all-files` and `uvx skilllint@latest check plugins/ .claude/` on PRs \u2014 the CI-level enforcement of the two local hooks above. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: same 